From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:10:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tokens: keep an account's credentials in one keychain item.

The keychain backend kept each credential in its own item, four for a signed-in account. macOS
trusts each item per build of the service, by code directory hash, so a new build asked for the
user's password four times per account. All credentials now live in one item, "credentials",
read once and then kept in memory: one prompt per account. Items created by another build are
deleted with SecKeychainItemDelete, because SecItemDelete refuses them. Credentials stored the old
way are not read: such an account signs in again.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: account
